WEBVTT

00:01:28.786 --> 00:01:30.192
is there's enough dust left over

00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:32.158
that it doesn't ignite into a star,

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.158
it becomes a planet.

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:38.983
And this is about a little over four billion years ago.

00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:40.416
And soon thereafter

00:01:40.416 --> 00:01:42.333
there's enough material left over

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:46.896
that you get a primordial soup,

00:01:46.896 --> 00:01:48.660
and that creates life.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.541
And life starts to expand and expand and expand,

00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:54.292
until it goes kaput.

00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:57.780
(Laughter)

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.210
Now the really strange thing

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:02.116
is life goes kaput, not once, not twice,